Package: barkvisor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Maintainer: BarkVisor Contributors <noreply@barkvisor.dev>
Homepage: https://github.com/pmdroid/barkvisor
Depends: libc6, ca-certificates, libcurl4 | libcurl4t64, libxml2, libsqlite3-0, libncurses6 | libncursesw6, libzstd1, libedit2, zlib1g, qemu-system-x86 | qemu-system-arm | qemu-system-aarch64 | qemu-kvm, qemu-utils, ovmf | qemu-efi-aarch64 | edk2-ovmf, genisoimage | xorriso | mkisofs, usbutils
Description: Headless QEMU VM manager with web UI
 BarkVisor is a headless daemon for managing QEMU virtual machines through
 a browser UI. Supports NAT and bridged networking, cloud images, cloud-init,
 serial console, and VNC on Linux arm64 and amd64 hosts.
 .
 This package installs the daemon under /usr/local, a systemd unit, and a
 default environment file. QEMU, UEFI firmware, ISO tools, and usbutils are
 required dependencies from the distro.
